  "entity_raw": {
    "name_raw": "Charging Hurler",
    "definition_type_raw": "Combat",
    "source_book_raw": "Ultimate Combat pg. 92",
    "definition_raw": "Source Ultimate Combat pg. 92\nYou know how to use your momentum to enhance your thrown weapon attacks.\n\nPrerequisites: Point-Blank Shot.\n\nBenefit: You can use the charge rules to make a thrown weapon attack. All the parameters of a charge apply, except that you must only move closer to your opponent, and you must end your movement within 30 feet of that opponent. If you do, you can make a single thrown weapon attack against that opponent, gaining the +2 bonus on the attack roll and taking a –2 penalty to your AC until the start of your next turn.",
