        "heading_raw": "Prerequisites",
        "body_raw": "Point-Blank Shot."
      },
      {
        "heading_raw": "Benefit",
        "body_raw": "You can use the charge rules to make a thrown weapon attack. All the parameters of a charge apply, except that you must only move closer to your opponent, and you must end your movement within 30 feet of that opponent. If you do, you can make a single thrown weapon attack against that opponent, gaining the +2 bonus on the attack roll and taking a –2 penalty to your AC until the start of your next turn."
      }
